    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{x-2}$. Find $f^{-1}(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{2x}{x-1}$, $x\\ne1$.",
      "worked": "Interchange $x$ and $y$ in $y=\\dfrac{x}{x-2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{y}{y-2}\\\\xy-2x&=y\\\\y(x-1)&=2x\\\\y&=\\frac{2x}{x-1}\\end{align*}$$\nHence $f^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{2x}{x-1}$, with domain $x\\ne1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
